--- title Times and dates
--- about Both do arithmetic with plain numbers, and what the number
--- about means differs: seconds for a time, days for a date. Both are
--- about read by path for their parts.

--- id times/adding-two-times
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1:00 + 1:00
--- result
2:00

--- id times/subtracting-two-times
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1:00 - 0:30
--- result
0:30

--- id times/a-time-can-be-negative
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note It is a duration rather than a clock reading, so there is no
--- note floor at midnight.
--- code
0:00 - 1:00
--- result
-1:00

--- id times/scaling-a-time
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1:00 * 2
--- result
2:00

--- id times/halving-a-time
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1:00 / 2
--- result
0:30

--- id times/a-bare-number-added-to-a-time-is-seconds
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Not minutes and not hours, which is the guess to get wrong.
--- code
1:00 + 1
--- result
1:00:01

--- id times/the-hour-of-a-time
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
t: 1:02:03
t/hour
--- result
1

--- id times/the-minute-of-a-time
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
t: 1:02:03
t/minute
--- result
2

--- id times/the-second-of-a-time
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
t: 1:02:03
t/second
--- result
3

--- id times/comparing-two-times
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1:00 < 2:00
--- result
#(true)

--- id times/converting-a-number-to-a-time-reads-it-as-seconds
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
to time! 60
--- result
0:01

--- id times/a-bare-number-added-to-a-date-is-days
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note A different unit from the time case, for the same spelling.
--- code
1-Jan-2020 + 1
--- result
2-Jan-2020

--- id times/stepping-a-date-back-over-a-year-boundary
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1-Jan-2020 - 1
--- result
31-Dec-2019

--- id times/the-days-between-two-dates
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note A whole number rather than a date, because the difference of
--- note two dates is a span and not a moment.
--- code
1-Jan-2020 - 1-Jan-2019
--- result
365

--- id times/the-year-of-a-date
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
d: 1-Jan-2020
d/year
--- result
2020

--- id times/the-month-of-a-date
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
d: 1-Jan-2020
d/month
--- result
1

--- id times/the-day-of-a-date
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
d: 1-Jan-2020
d/day
--- result
1

--- id times/comparing-two-dates
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1-Jan-2020 < 2-Jan-2020
--- result
#(true)

--- id times/a-time-as-a-number-is-its-seconds
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
to integer! 1:00
--- result
3600

--- id times/a-time-can-be-asked-whether-it-is-zero
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
zero? 0:00
--- result
#(true)

--- id times/a-negative-time-is-negative
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
negative? -1:00
--- result
#(true)

--- id times/rounding-a-time
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
round 1:00
--- result
1:00

--- id times/a-part-a-time-has-not-got
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note A time raises where a date answers none, so the two are not
--- note the same rule with different field names.
--- code
t: 1:00
t/nonesuch
--- error script invalid-path

--- id times/a-part-a-date-has-not-got
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
d: 1-Jan-2020
d/nonesuch
--- result
_

--- id times/a-time-is-indexable-too
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Position 1 is the hour, so the named and numbered spellings
--- note agree the way they do for a pair.
--- code
t: 1:00
t/1
--- result
1

--- id times/a-time-equals-its-seconds
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which makes EQUAL? cross the datatype boundary here, as it
--- note does for integers and decimals.
--- code
1:00 = 3600
--- result
#(true)
